@startuml
!theme cyborg
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F4F6
skinparam ArrowColor #CBD5E1
title HISTORICAL broader-product proposal — Optional Kubernetes-style alternative — not adopted for the initial candidate
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Cluster control plane\nNot provisioned; operating cost / compatibility gate" as CP
node "Trusted workload cluster candidate" {
 rectangle "Namespace: trusted-app (illustrative)" {
  rectangle "Web Deployment -> web Pods\nScoped service identity / resources" as W
  rectangle "Worker Deployment -> worker Pods\nExact attempts / claim guards" as J
  rectangle "Scheduler job responsibility\nOverlap / uniqueness controls" as S
 }
 rectangle "Service / ingress controller\nImplementation / policy pending" as I
 I --> W
}
rectangle "External or separately evaluated isolated executor\nNamespace alone is not untrusted-code containment" as E #164E63
rectangle "Durable database / private storage\nPersistence and recovery separately evaluated" as D
CP ..> W : desired-state control
W --> D
J --> D
J --> E : gated scope only
legend bottom
 Clusters, namespaces, Pods and Deployments illustrate a possible orchestration mapping only.
 No replicas, node sizes, manifests, storage class or network-policy implementation is selected.
 A namespace/container label cannot prove hostile job isolation, cross-tenant privacy or HA.
endlegend
@enduml
